+/// does this unless the text has a character with a shorter equivalent (`text_can_shrink`,
+/// worked out once per search, in `can_shrink`): a group is a piece of the text, so without one
+/// no group can match fewer bytes than it has. That keeps `(é+)\1`, which tries the reference
+/// once for every length of the group, at one comparison and not one per length.
+fn casei_backref_end<S: HaystackInput + ?Sized>(
